- Task: NL -> symbolic formula generation (physics/mathematics)

Intended Use
-------------
- Assistive generation of symbolic formulas from short natural language descriptions.
- NOT intended for making critical engineering/clinical/financial decisions without human review.

Data
----
- Training data: mix of synthetic templates and curated labeled pairs (description -> canonical_formula).
- Data sources and provenance must be recorded in the dataset manifest.

Evaluation
----------
- Metrics used: parse success rate (sympy), dimensional-validity rate (domain validator), BLEU, composite metric.

Safety & Limitations
--------------------
- Model can hallucinate physically incorrect formulas even when fluent; always validate with domain rules (sympy + dimension checks).
- Not all mathematical notations are supported; canonicalization is required.
